      {
        "id": 139935,
        "name": "Azqa",
        "username": "Azqa",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/azqa/{size}/2015_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-04-28T15:55:33.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"ScarecrowKing\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/letter_avatar_proxy/v4/letter/s/919ad9/48.png\" class=\"avatar\"> ScarecrowKing:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Now that I have DW Fixer, though,&nbsp;I'm realizing that his base power sucks so bad!</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>I really thought that I'd like DW Fixer more than regular because of the times I lamented regular Fixer's low raw damage output. &nbsp;I've since found that I tend to prefer being able to keep things in play for more than one turn, so preference of character version becomes very situationally dependent on the villain and teammates.</p>",
